{"id":129,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"A feeble, pitiful imbecile of a Pokémon that is nonetheless very hardy. Unperturbed by turbid water, it can be found living in all sorts of places."},{"games":["Shield","Crystal"],"text":"This weak and pathetic Pokémon gets easily pushed along rivers when there are strong currents."},{"games":["Sword","X","FireRed"],"text":"It is virtually worthless in terms of both power and speed. It is the most weak and pathetic Pokémon in the world."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"Famous for being very unreliable. It can be found swimming in seas, lakes, rivers, and shallow puddles."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Thanks to their strong hold on life, dirty water doesn’t bother them at all. They live in waters all over the world!"},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"In the distant past, they were fairly strong, but they have become gradually weaker over time."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"Its reckless leaps make it easy pickings for predators. On the bright side, many Pokémon enjoy longer life spans, thanks to Magikarp."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Although weak and helpless, this Pokémon is incredibly fertile. They exist in such multitudes, you’ll soon grow tired of seeing them."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Magikarp is virtually useless in battle as it can only splash around. As a result, it is considered to be weak. However, it is actually a very hardy Pokémon that can survive in any body of water no matter how polluted it is."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Magikarp is a pathetic excuse for a Pokémon that is only capable of flopping and splashing. This behavior prompted scientists to undertake research into it."},{"games":["Y","LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"In the distant past, it was somewhat stronger than the horribly weak descendants that exist today."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"A Magikarp living for many years can leap a mountain using Splash. The move remains useless, though."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"For no reason, it jumps and splashes about, making it easy for predators like PIDGEOTTO to catch it mid-jump."},{"games":["HeartGold"],"text":"An underpowered, pathetic Pokémon. It may jump high on rare occasions, but usually not more than seven feet."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Swift Swim","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in rain."},{"name":"Rattled","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon gets scared when hit by a Dark-, Ghost-, or Bug-type attack or if intimidated, which boosts its Speed stat."}],"eggGroups":["Water 2","Dragon"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":5,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"water's edge","color":"Red","shape":"Fish","evolution":{"id":129,"name":"Magikarp","condition":null,"children":[{"id":130,"name":"Gyarados","condition":"Lv. 20","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,150],[15,33],[25,175]],"machine":[],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me55c-203","name":"Magikarp","set":"30th Celebration: Classic Collection","date":"2026-09-16","rarity":"Illustration Rare","number":"203","artist":"Shinji Kanda","small":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55c-203/small","large":"https://images.scrydex.com/pokemon/me55c-203/large"},{"id":"sv10-48","name":"Misty's Magikarp","set":"Destined Rivals","date":"2025-05-30","rarity":"Common","number":"48","artist":null,"img":"sv10/48"},{"id":"sv3pt5-129","name":"Magikarp","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Common","number":"129","artist":"Kouki Saitou","img":"sv3pt5/129"},{"id":"sv2-42","name":"Magikarp","set":"Paldea Evolved","date":"2023-06-09","rarity":"Common","number":"42","artist":"HYOGONOSUKE","img":"sv2/42"},{"id":"sv2-203","name":"Magikarp","set":"Paldea Evolved","date":"2023-06-09","rarity":"Illustration Rare","number":"203","artist":"Shinji Kanda","img":"sv2/203"},{"id":"sv1-44","name":"Magikarp","set":"Scarlet & Violet","